  "details": "Just an idea that would allow people to get more creative with avatars and actually allow creators to prevent prevent underage users from even using features they feel aren't intended for minors.\n\nAdd a checkbox on contacts/physbones or potentially any script on an avatar to lock the interaction to an age verified individual should the avatar somehow manage to be around/in the use of people  who shouldn't be around it.\n\nExamples:\n\n18+ tag on a material making the object with said material invisible to underage users. \n\n18+ tag on collider tied to suggestive animation/sound, etc preventing it from being interacted with should it be accidentally touched by anyone.\n\n18+ tag on a physbone chain because that is not okay to have out in polite company in the first place why is that there. \n\nThese can togglable in menus for verified users to enable/disable the visibility of, and simply not available to unverified users. Avatar creators/editors may choose to add/remove them at their own risk.  \n\nIt is recommended that extensive testing features are included with this to prevent them from accidentally being misplaced and that there be an option to 'preview 18+ content' be provided be provided to the user before any uploaded involved with these features.",
